Report a change of the sub-menu close delay

settingsChanged() compares every input of the dialog against the stored
configuration, and updateChanged() gates the live preview and the
changed signal on that answer. The sub-menu close delay box had no
comparison, so a user who moved only that box saw no preview and left
the Apply button asleep.

The close delay now joins its sibling, the sub-menu delay, in the
comparison.

The change sits on the branch work/dialog-state of the local tree, as commit 7 of 12.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index 1dbbd8db..d84c073a 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -3927,6 +3927,7 @@ bool QtCurveConfig::settingsChanged(const Options &opts)
          lighterPopupMenuBgnd->value()!=opts.lighterPopupMenuBgnd ||
          tabBgnd->value()!=opts.tabBgnd ||
          menuDelay->value()!=opts.menuDelay ||
+         menuCloseDelay->value()!=opts.menuCloseDelay ||
          sliderWidth->value()!=opts.sliderWidth ||
          menuStripe->currentIndex()!=opts.menuStripe ||
          menuStripeAppearance->currentIndex()!=opts.menuStripeAppearance ||
